| Order | File under `delivery/` | Focus |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | `messaging/DeliveryCommand.java` | Message sent from A to B; immutable dispatch configuration and validation. |
| 2 | `persistence/DeliveryProjectionStore.java` — `delivery()` | Initial delivery row created during ingestion/replay. Leave `applyStatus()` for step 6. |
| 3 | `outbox/Outbox.java` | Read `enqueue()` first, then `publishPending()`: database insert → claim pending row → publish → broker confirmation → mark published. |

| 4 | `messaging/DeliveryStatusMessage.java` | Final result B sends back to A. |
| 5 | `messaging/StatusListener.java` → `StatusUpdateService.java` | Receive, validate, apply transactionally, then acknowledge; follow reject/requeue handling. |
| 6 | `persistence/DeliveryProjectionStore.java` — `applyStatus()` | Deduplicate status messages and update delivery/attempt projections. |

| 7 | `reconciliation/ReconciliationWorker.java` | Scheduled entry point for repairing missed status updates. |
| 8 | `reconciliation/ReconciliationService.java` | Read checkpoint → fetch completion page → apply results → advance checkpoint atomically. |
| 9 | `client/DeliveryCompletionClient.java` | Actual REST call to B, internal credential, and timeouts. |


